Sval: a nested Cocoa event loop hands its Gecko wake-up to the loop around it

Backport of Mozilla's Bug 1705365 (mozilla-central 305e4f921351 and its test
2f8880339bc1, Firefox 161), unchanged. ESR 153 does not carry it.
nsAppShell::ProcessGeckoEvents wakes a waiting native loop by clearing
mRunningEventLoop. When a native event's handler spins a nested Gecko loop,
the nested ProcessNextNativeEvent consumed that wake-up, then restored
mRunningEventLoop to true on its way out, so the enclosing native loop went
back to waiting with Gecko events pending until some unrelated native event
arrived. The test adds nsICocoaAppShellTestUtils, which posts a native event
and counts wake-ups lost this way, and test_nested_native_loop_wakeup_mac.html.
Drop this patch when the upstream pin reaches Firefox 161.

